#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "mound of dirt"
msgstr "butte de terre"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An area of heaped dirt, not easily traversable.  If examined more closely, "
"it's quite favorable for planting seeds and the like."
msgstr ""
"Un monticule de terre, assez difficile à traverser, mais un bon endroit ou "
"planter des graines."

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A giant hill of dirt that looks like you could crawl inside for shelter."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "odd fault"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "odd fault"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An unnaturally humanoid-shaped hole, it seems oddly familiar.  You feel a "
"strange urge to examine it closer, as if it belongs to you somehow."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message about the player in an effect
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"This wall is perfectly vertical.  Odd, twisted holes are set in it, leading "
"as far back into the solid rock as you can see.  The holes are humanoid in "
"shape, but with long, twisted, distended limbs."
msgstr ""
"Ce mur est parfaitement vertical. Il est percé de trous étranges et tordus "
"qui s'enfoncent aussi loin que possible dans la roche solide. Les trous ont "
"une forme humanoïde, mais avec des membres longs, tordus et distendus."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "grave"
msgstr "tombe"

#. ~ Description of terrain "grave"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A dirt grave, with some grass growing on it.  At least some of the dead do "
"actually rest in peace."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "grave"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A fresh grave, covered with stones, either to keep something from digging it"
" up or to keep one inside from digging out of it.  Or both.  Two planks mark"
" this place of someone's eternal rest."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "rubber mulch"
msgstr "paillis de caoutchouc"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rubber mulch"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large area mulched with shredded rubber.  It's a softer place to land than"
" regular dirt."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "pavement"
msgstr "chaussée"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A segment of asphalt, slowly degrading from cracks, frost heaves, and lack "
"of maintenance."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "yellow pavement"
msgstr "chaussée jaune"

#. ~ Description of terrain "yellow pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Streaks of carefully aligned yellow paint mark the road to inform drivers "
"not to cross.  No one is enforcing these rules anymore."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "pedestrian crossing"
msgstr "passage à piétons"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pedestrian crossing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"White polymer lines painted on the pavement which indicate places where "
"pedestrians should cross the road."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "sidewalk"
msgstr "trottoir"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sidewalk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An area of common poured concrete, damaged by frost heaves and large cracks "
"due to lack of maintenance."
msgstr ""
"Une zone de béton coulé commun, endommagée par des coups de gel et de "
"grandes fissures dues à un manque d'entretien."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "concrete"
msgid_plural "concrete"
msgstr[0] "béton"
msgstr[1] "béton"
msgstr[2] "béton"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A newer segment of poured concrete with surface finishes for aesthetics and "
"resistance to freeze-thaw cycles."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A newer segment of poured concrete with surface finishes for aesthetics and "
"resistance to freeze-thaw cycles.  Covered with a streak of yellow paint."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "wooden floor"
msgstr "sol en bois"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A wooden floor created from boards, packed tightly together and nailed down."
"  Common on patios."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "wooden floor gangway"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor gangway"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A wooden gangway bridging a short gap.  Sturdy enough to act as a floor, but"
" not sufficient to support additional flooring."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"High-quality and tough checkered metal flooring to reduce the risk of slips "
"and falls."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "metal floor gangway"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor gangway"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A metal gangway bridging a short gap.  Sturdy enough to act as a floor, but "
"not sufficient to support additional flooring."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "dirt floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A floor consisting of finely mixed earth that has been tamped down."
msgstr ""
"Une section de sol consistant de terre ayant été pulvérisée puis tassée."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "gelatinous ground"
msgstr "sol gélatineux"

#. ~ Description of terrain "gelatinous ground"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An incursion of a large area of otherworldly substrate, it feels like "
"walking on hardened gelatin."
msgstr ""
"Une incursion de sol extradimensional donnant l'impression d'être "
"entièrement composé de gélatine durcie."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "orifice"
msgstr "orifice"

#. ~ Description of terrain "orifice"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large round orifice, with trails of fresh and dried-up strange green "
"liquid with a strongly acidic odor covering its inner sides."
msgstr ""
"Un orifice sphérique, des trainées d'un liquide vert étrange en train de "
"sécher recouvrant l'intérieur."

#. ~ Description of terrain "elevator"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "An elevator section of the flight deck."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "deck coating"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thick metal hull coating, covered with a military-grade epoxy mix.  Used "
"for runways, and can't be melted by jet engine nozzles."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "yellow deck coating"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "yellow deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thick metal hull covering, covered with a military-grade epoxy mix and "
"painted yellow."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "red deck coating"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "red deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thick metal hull covering, covered with a military-grade epoxy mix, and "
"painted red."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "white deck coating"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "white deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A thick metal hull covering, covered with a military-grade epoxy mix and "
"painted white."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "walnut tree"
msgstr "noyer"

#. ~ Description of terrain "walnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested walnuts."
msgstr ""
"Un arbre massif appartenant au genre \"Juglans\". En regardant de plus près,"
" vous observez des noix ayant l'air récoltables."

#. ~ Description of terrain "walnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus."
msgstr "Un arbre massif appartenant au genre \"Juglans\"."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "butternut tree"
msgstr "noyer cendré"

#. ~ Description of terrain "butternut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus, but with lighter bark and "
"more elongated fruits than the more common black walnut.  If you look "
"closely, you can see some unharvested butternuts."
msgstr ""
"Un arbre massif appartenant au genre \"Juglans\", son écorce étant plus "
"claire et ses fruits plus allongés que le noyer noir plus répandu. Vous "
"observez quelques noix douces pouvant être récoltées."

#. ~ Description of terrain "butternut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus, but with lighter bark and "
"more elongated fruits than the more common black walnut."
msgstr ""
"Un arbre massif appartenant au genre \"Juglans\", son écorce étant plus "
"claire et ses fruits plus allongés que le noyer noir plus répandu."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "blackjack oak"
msgstr "chêne noir"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackjack oak"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the genus 'Quercus', with bark cracked into rectangular "
"black plates split by narrow orange fissures.  You could peel off the bark "
"sections if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Arbre à feuilles caduques du genre \"Quercus\", dont l'écorce est fendue en "
"plaques rectangulaires noires séparées par d'étroites fissures orange. En "
"examinant l'arbre de plus près, on peut décoller les parties de l'écorce."

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackjack oak"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the genus 'Quercus', with bark cracked into rectangular "
"black plates split by narrow orange fissures.  All the usable bark has been "
"stripped off."
msgstr ""
"Un arbre à feuilles caduques du genre \"Quercus\", dont l'écorce est "
"fissurée en plaques rectangulaires noires séparées par d'étroites fissures "
"oranges. Toute l'écorce utilisable a été enlevée."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "alder tree"
msgstr "aulne"

#. ~ Description of terrain "alder tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous flowering tree with serrated, scalloped, round-obovate leaves, "
"commonly forming dense groves alongside water."
msgstr ""
"Un arbre à fleurs aux feuilles rondes-obovales caduques, dentelées et "
"festonnées formant habituellement de denses bosquets le long de plans d'eau."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/furniture_and_terrain/tropical_terrain_flora.json
msgid "chestnut tree"
msgstr "châtaignier"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chestnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Castanea' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested chestnuts."
msgstr ""
"Un arbre massif appartenant au genre \"Castanea\". En regardant de plus "
"près, vous observez des châtaignes ayant l'air récoltables."

#. ~ Description of terrain "chestnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Castanea' genus."
msgstr "Un arbre massif appartenant au genre \"Castanea\"."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "beech tree"
msgstr "hêtre"

#. ~ Description of terrain "beech tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Fagus' genus.  If you look closely, you can"
" see some unharvested beech nuts."
msgstr ""
"Un arbre massif appartenant au genre \"Fagus\". En regardant de plus près, "
"vous observez des faînes ayant l'air récoltables."

#. ~ Description of terrain "beech tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Fagus' genus."
msgstr "Un arbre massif appartenant au genre \"Fagus\"."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "hazelnut tree"
msgstr "noisetier"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hazelnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A stubby tree belonging to the 'Corylus' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested hazelnuts."
msgstr ""
"Un arbre trapu appartenant au genre \"Corylus\". En regardant de plus près, "
"vous observez des noisettes ayant l'air récoltables."

#. ~ Description of terrain "hazelnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A stubby tree belonging to the 'Corylus' genus."
msgstr "Un arbre trapu appartenant au genre \"Corylus\"."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "oak tree"
msgstr "chêne"

#. ~ Description of terrain "oak tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found "
"throughout the New England region.  If you look closely, you can see some "
"acorns the squirrels haven't gotten yet."
msgstr ""
"Un arbre aux feuilles caduques massif appartenant au genre \"Quercus\", un "
"arbre commun à travers la Nouvelle Angleterre. Vous observez quelques glands"
" mûrs n'ayant pas encore été touchés par les écureuils."

#. ~ Description of terrain "oak tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found "
"throughout the New England region."
msgstr ""
"Un arbre aux feuilles caduques massif appartenant au genre \"Quercus\", un "
"arbre commun à travers la Nouvelle Angleterre."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "basswood tree"
msgstr "tilleul"

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the "
"summer, and you might be able to eat its young leaves in the spring."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the "
"summer, and its edible young leaves have already been harvested."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "cottonwood tree"
msgstr "peuplier"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cottonwood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Populus' genus, commonly found throughout the"
" New England region.  You see some cottonwood tree bolls that can be "
"harvested."
msgstr ""
"Un grand arbre appartenant au genre \"Populus, un arbre commun à travers la "
"Nouvelle Angleterre. Vous observez quelque capsules à votre portée que vous "
"pourriez récolter."

#. ~ Description of terrain "cottonwood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Populus' genus, commonly found throughout the"
" New England region.  All the cottonwood tree bolls have been harvested."
msgstr ""
"Un grand arbre appartenant au genre \"Populus, un arbre commun à travers la "
"Nouvelle Angleterre. Toute les capsules à votre portée ont été récoltées."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "elm tree"
msgstr "orme"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elm tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Ulmus' genus, commonly found throughout the "
"New England region."
msgstr ""
"Un large arbre appartenant au genre \"Ulmus\", un arbre commun à travers la "
"nouvelle angleterre."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead tree"
msgstr "arbre mort"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An indiscernible tree that has withered away due to weather, fire, or "
"otherworldly causes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An indiscernible tree that has withered away due to weather, fire, or "
"otherworldly causes.  Someone or something has broken most of its dead "
"branches, leaving little but its gnarled trunk."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "warped dead tree"
msgstr "arbre mort déformé"

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This deciduous tree's branches are warped into a spiral.  This appears to "
"have killed it."
msgstr ""
"Les branches de cet arbre à feuilles caduques ont été transformée en "
"spirales, ce processus l'ayant apparemment tué."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "young tree"
msgstr "jeune arbre"

#. ~ Description of terrain "young tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A relatively young sapling of an indeterminate species.  It could take "
"decades before reaching maturity, so there's no use waiting around."
msgstr ""
"Un arbre relativement jeune dont l'espèce est encore difficile à déterminer."
" Cela pourrait prendre des décennies avant qu'ils soit mature, donc ne "
"restez pas planté(e) là à l'attendre."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "mega fern"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "mega fern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A gigantic fern like nothing you've seen before.  The leaves are a bright "
"scarlet with a net-like structure of green veins.  The multipronged trunks "
"have the texture of balsa wood."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "apple tree"
msgstr "pommier"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as apples.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably "
"find a few mature ones in autumn."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as apples.  There do not appear to be any ripe apples now."
msgstr ""
"Un membre du genre \"Malus\", cet arbre produit des fruits communément "
"connus sous le nom de pommes. Il n'y a pas l'air d'avoir de pommes mûres "
"dessus en ce moment."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pear tree"
msgstr "poirier"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces fruit in "
"the fall.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably "
"find a few mature ones."
msgstr ""
"Un \"Pyrus communis\" ou poirier commun, produisant ses fruits durant "
"l'automne. Si vous examiniez ses branches de plus près, vous pourriez "
"probablement en trouver plusieurs assez mûres."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces fruit in "
"the fall.  Looks like all the ripe pears have been picked."
msgstr ""
"Un \"Pyrus communis\" ou poirier commun, produisant ses fruits durant "
"l'automne. On dirait que toutes les poires mûres ont déjà été cueillies."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "coffee tree"
msgstr "arbre à café du kentucky"

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'gymnocladus dioicus', or the kentucky coffee tree, which produces "
"roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  If you examined the "
"branches more closely, you could probably find a few mature ones."
msgstr ""
"Un membre de l'espèce \"gymnocladus dioicus\", connu sous le nom de caféier "
"du Kentucky, produisant des fèves durant l'automne pouvant être grillées et "
"pressées pour produire un liquide assez similaire en goût au véritable café."
" Si vous examiniez ses branches de plus près, vous pourriez probablement "
"trouver un bon nombre de fèves prêtes à être récoltées."

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'gymnocladus dioicus', or the kentucky coffee tree, which produces "
"roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  Looks like all the "
"ripe pods have been picked."
msgstr ""
"Un membre de l'espèce \"gymnocladus dioicus\", connu sous le nom de caféier "
"du Kentucky, produisant des fèves durant l'automne pouvant être grillées et "
"pressées pour produire un liquide assez similaire en goût au véritable café."
" On dirait que toutes les fèves assez mûres on déjà été récoltées."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "cherry tree"
msgstr "cerisier"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"cherries in the summer.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could"
" probably find some viable clusters."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"cherries in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of cherries have "
"been picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "juniper tree"
msgstr "genévrier"

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries"
" grow over two to three years.  It flowers in the first year, produces a "
"green berry the second, and in the third produces the more famed blue "
"varieties.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could probably "
"find some viable clusters."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries"
" grow over two to three years.  It flowers in the first year, produces a "
"green berry the second, and in the third produces the more famed blue "
"varieties.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of berries have been picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "peach tree"
msgstr "pêcher"

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"peaches in the summer.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could"
" probably find some mature peaches."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"peaches in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe peaches have been picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "apricot tree"
msgstr "abricotier"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apricot tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A transplanted species of 'Prunus armeniaca', rarely found in New England.  "
"It produces apricots in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely,"
" you could probably find some mature apricots."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "apricot tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A transplanted species of 'Prunus armeniaca', rarely found in New England.  "
"It produces apricots in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe apricots have "
"been picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "plum tree"
msgstr "prunier"

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it "
"produces plums in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely, you "
"could probably find some ripe plums."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it "
"produces plums in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe plums have been "
"picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "mulberry tree"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as mulberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as mulberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe mulberries now."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "elderberry tree"
msgstr "sureau"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly "
"known as elderberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr ""
"Cet arbre est un membre du genre \"Sambucus\", et produit des baies "
"communément connues comme baies de sureau durant l'été."

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly "
"known as elderberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe elderberries now."
msgstr ""
"Cet arbre est un membre du genre \"Sambucus\", et produit des baies "
"communément connues comme baies de sureau durant l'été. Il n'y a pas l'air "
"d'avoir de baies mûres en ce moment."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pine tree"
msgstr "sapin"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"If you examined the tree more closely, you might find usable sticky whorls, "
"resin clumps, and pinecones."
msgstr ""
"Un conifère imposant appartenant aux genre \"Pinus\", et celui-ci faisant "
"probablement partie d'une des trois espèces les plus répandues en Nouvelle "
"Angleterre, \"P. strobus\",\"P. resinosa\" ou \"P. rigida\". Si vous "
"inspectiez l'arbre de plus près, vous pourriez probablement trouver des "
"spirales suintant de la résine de pin utile, des amas de résine et des "
"pommes de pin."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"Some of the branches and resin clumps have been stripped away and many of "
"the pinecones aren't developed fully yet, but given a season, it could be "
"harvestable again."
msgstr ""
"Un conifère imposant appartenant aux genre \"Pinus\", et celui-ci faisant "
"probablement partie d'une des trois espèces les plus répandues en Nouvelle "
"Angleterre, \"P. strobus\",\"P. resinosa\" ou \"P. rigida\". Cet arbre à "
"l'air d'avoir été débarrassé de la majorité de ces pommes de pin et de sa "
"résine facilement accessible, mais sera probablement capable de produire "
"plus si vous attendez une saison."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead pine tree"
msgstr "sapin mort"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"This tree's branches are bare, and it appears to be dead."
msgstr ""
"Un conifère imposant appartenant aux genre \"Pinus\", et celui-ci faisant "
"probablement partie d'une des trois espèces les plus répandues en Nouvelle "
"Angleterre, \"P. strobus\",\"P. resinosa\" ou \"P. rigida\". Ses branches "
"sont nues et l'arbre à l'air d'être mort."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "warped dead pine tree"
msgstr "pin mort déformé"

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The branches of this pine tree have been twisted into a shape that remind "
"you of Sierpinski triangles.  It did not survive being warped like this."
msgstr ""
"Les branches de cet arbre ont été altérées jusqu'à ce qu'elle ressemblent "
"une forme qui rappellent les triangles de Sierpinski, l'arbre n'ayant pas "
"survécu cette transformation traumatique."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "birch tree"
msgstr "bouleau"

#. ~ Description of terrain "birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Betula' genus, with the characteristic peeling"
" bark.  Species like 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera', and 'B. "
"populifolia' are the most common in the New England region.  You could tear "
"off some strips of bark if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Betula' genus, with the characteristic peeling"
" bark.  Species like 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera', and 'B. "
"populifolia' are the most common in the New England region.  Looks like "
"there isn't enough rhytidome to peel off yet."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "willow tree"
msgstr "saule"

#. ~ Description of terrain "willow tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall, wide deciduous tree of the 'Salix' genus, with long, thin, leafy "
"branches that hang down like curtains.  You could tear off some bark."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "willow tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall, wide deciduous tree of the 'Salix' genus, with long, thin, leafy "
"branches that hang down like curtains.  Looks like all usable bark has been "
"torn off, and new rhytidomes have not formed yet."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "maple tree"
msgstr "érable"

#. ~ Description of terrain "maple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large deciduous tree of the 'Acer' genus.  The leaves are distinctively "
"shaped with five prongs.  It could be tapped in order to extract maple sap."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "maple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large deciduous tree of the 'Acer' genus.  The leaves are distinctively "
"shaped with five prongs.  A spigot is wedged into the trunk, and sweet maple"
" sap can be extracted."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "hickory tree"
msgstr "caryer"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  You could look for hickory nuts"
" if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  It looks like the tree has been"
" picked clean of hickory nuts."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pistachio tree"
msgstr "pistachier"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pistachio tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Pistacia' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is"
" not native to this region.  You could look for pistachio nuts if you "
"examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "pistachio tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Pistacia' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is"
" not native to this region.  Unfortunately, it looks like it has been picked"
" clean of pistachio nuts."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "almond tree"
msgstr "amandier"

#. ~ Description of terrain "almond tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Prunus' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is "
"not native to this region.  You could look for fresh almonds if you examined"
" the tree more closely."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "almond tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Prunus' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is "
"not native to this region.  There are no almonds left to pick on the tree."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pecan tree"
msgstr "pacanier"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pecan tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  You could look for pecan nuts "
"if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "pecan tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  It doesn't look like there are "
"any pecan nuts left on the tree."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead hickory tree"
msgstr "caryer mort"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The dead remnants of a tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  Nothing "
"useful can be foraged from this poor, dead tree."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "sassafras tree"
msgstr "sassafras"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sassafras tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sassafras' genus, known for its aromatic "
"qualities.  In the winter and spring, the sap rich roots can be harvested to"
" make a sweet beverage."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of terrain "sassafras tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sassafras' genus, known for its aromatic "
"qualities.  This tree's roots have been harvested, any more and the tree "
"will die."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "underbrush"
msgid_plural "underbrushes"
msgstr[0] "sous-bois"
msgstr[1] "sous-bois"
msgstr[2] "sous-bois"

#. ~ Description of terrain "underbrush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Small plants and shrubs that decorate the forest.  An observant forager "
"could obtain edible plants, acorns, eggs, and mushrooms from it."
msgstr ""
"Petites plantes et arbustes qui décorent la forêt. Un observateur avisé "
"pourrait en obtenir des plantes comestibles, des glands, des œufs et des "
"champignons."

#. ~ Description of terrain "underbrush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Small plants and shrubs that decorate the forest.  It has been rummaged "
"through and doesn't have anything useful left to forage from it."
msgstr ""
"Les petites plantes, mousses et buissons poussant sur le sol d'une forêt. "
"Cette zone a déjà été fouillée et il n'y a rien d'autre d'intéressant à "
"ramasser ici."

#. ~ Description of terrain "underbrush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Small plants and shrubs that decorate the forest.  It has been rummaged "
"through and doesn't have anything useful left to forage from it.  Frost "
"covers it."
msgstr ""
"Les petites plantes, mousses et buissons poussant sur le sol d'une forêt, "
"tous couverts d'une fine couche de gel. Cette zone a déjà été fouillée et il"
" n'y a rien d'autre d'intéressant à ramasser ici."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/mods/alt_map_key/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "bee hive"
msgstr "ruche"

#. ~ Description of terrain "bee hive"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A hive of bees located in a cavity inside a tree, swarming in and out at a "
"feverish pace.  There's probably honey inside."
msgstr ""
"Une ruche d'abeilles situé dans une cavité d'arbre, les habitantes "
"bourdonnant autour de l'entrée sans jamais s'épuiser. Il y a peut être du "
"miel à récolter à l'intérieur si vous possédez un moyen de les assommer ou "
"ne craignez pas leur colère."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "apiary"
msgstr "ruche"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apiary"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A man-made wooden box designed to hold honeybees and facilitate the care for"
" a hive.  The modular construction allows for inspecting the bees and "
"harvesting their bounty without destroying the hive completely.  This year's"
" harvest should be ready by now."
msgstr ""
"Une boite en bois fabriquée pour accueillir des abeilles à miel et "
"simplifiez l'entretien par un apiculteur de leur ruche. La construction "
"modulaire permet d'inspécter la santé des abeilles et récolter leur miel "
"sans détruire leur colonie complétement. La récolte de cette année à l'air "
"d'être prête."

#. ~ Description of terrain "apiary"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A man-made wooden box designed to host honeybees and facilitate the care for"
" a hive.  The modular construction allows for inspecting the bees and "
"harvesting their bounty without destroying the hive completely.  It will be "
"some time before this one is ready to harvest."
msgstr ""
"Une boite en bois fabriquée pour accueillir des abeilles à miel et "
"simplifiez l'entretien par un apiculteur de leur ruche. La construction "
"modulaire permet d'inspécter la santé des abeilles et récolter leur miel "
"sans détruire leur colonie complétement. Vous allez devoir patienter un bon "
"moment avant que le miel de celle-ci soit prêt à être récolté."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "shrub"
msgstr "arbuste"

#. ~ Description of terrain "shrub"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A small shrub."
msgstr "Un petit buisson."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
