msgid ""
"The British empire's standard combat cartridge throughout the nineteenth and"
" twentieth centuries, first as a bottlenecked black powder design before "
"evolving into a spitzered, smokeless round, this is a modern produced .303 "
"caliber cartridge.  Loaded with a single core, 180gr soft-point bullet, the "
"projectile features an open-tipped design manufactured from lead.  This "
"loading allows the round to undergo greater expansion upon striking targets,"
