msgstr[1] "fusils de combat Mosin"
msgstr[2] "fusils de combat Mosin"

#. ~ Description of gun "Mosin battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"Developed by the Russian Empire prior to the onset of the First World War, "
"the Mosin is a bolt-action military battle rifle chambered for 7.62x54mm "
"rounds.  Powerful, unwieldy, and prolific across the world as military "
"surplus, this sizable rifle is a Soviet updated version of the venerable "
"Mosin."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Mosin battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30"
msgid_plural "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30"
msgstr[0] "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30"
msgstr[1] "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30"
msgstr[2] "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30"

#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin battle rifle" of gun "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"The Mosin-Nagant 1891/30 is a bolt-action, internal magazine-fed military "
"rifle, developed by the Russian Empire and later used and perfected by the "
"Soviet Union."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Mosin battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30-EBR"
msgid_plural "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30-EBR"
msgstr[0] "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30-EBR"
msgstr[1] "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30-EBR"
msgstr[2] "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30-EBR"

#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin battle rifle" of gun "Mosin-Nagant
#. 1891/30-EBR"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"This Mosin-Nagant has exchanged the classic wooden stock for a modern "
"synthetic model, carefully balanced to the same weight and handling, to "
"allow support for modern accessories."
msgstr ""

