msgid_plural "bowfins"
msgstr[0] "poisson-castor"
msgstr[1] "poissons-castors"
msgstr[2] "poissons-castors"

#. ~ Description of monster "bowfin"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A bowfin.  These fish are related to gar but without the huge teeth, skin-"
"rending scales, and aggression."
msgstr ""
"Un poisson-castor, un cousin du brochet dépourvu de son agressivité, de ses "
"dents pointues, écailles coupantes, mais ayant reçu en compensation une tête"
" couverte de longues plaques osseuses."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "longnose gar"
msgid_plural "longnose gars"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "longnose gar"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A large ancient type of fish with a mean jaw and poisonous eggs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "burbot"
msgid_plural "burbots"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "burbot"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A relatively large fish that looks like a cross between a catfish and an "
"eel, and is the only freshwater fish from the order that cods hail from."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "lake sturgeon"
msgid_plural "lake sturgeons"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "lake sturgeon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A very large armored bottom-feeder, the lake sturgeon is one of the largest "
"unmutated fish one can find in the freshwater regions of New England."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "shortnose sturgeon"
msgid_plural "shortnose sturgeons"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "shortnose sturgeon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"While the shortnose sturgeon is still large, it is nothing compared to its "
"cousin - the lake sturgeon.  What really sets it apart, however, is its "
"signature shorter snout."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "fallfish"
msgid_plural "fallfish"
msgstr[0] "ouitouche"
msgstr[1] "ouitouches"
msgstr[2] "ouitouches"

#. ~ Description of monster "fallfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A fallfish.  These fish are small cyprinids, related to carp."
msgstr "Un ouitouche, un petit cyprinidé apparenté aux carpes."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "lobster"
msgid_plural "lobsters"
msgstr[0] "homard"
msgstr[1] "homards"
msgstr[2] "homards"

#. ~ Description of monster "lobster"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A dark greenish crustacean in its natural habitat.  These were once "
"considered pests barely worth eating, then some marketing genius started "
"selling them to people as a delicacy and they took off in popularity… and "
"price."
msgstr ""
"Un crustacé noir verdâtre dans son habitat naturel. Autrefois considérés "
"nuisibles et valant à peine d'être mangés, un génie du marketing décida un "
"jour de les vendre comme un met raffiné, causant ceux-ci à gagner en "
"popularité… et en prix."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "crayfish"
msgid_plural "crayfish"
msgstr[0] "écrevisse"
msgstr[1] "écrevisses"
msgstr[2] "écrevisses"

#. ~ Description of monster "crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"This crustacean looks like a tiny lobster, but is actually a completely "
"different species.  If you could get ahold of a bunch more of these, a hefty"
" pot of boiling water, and some spicy seasonings…"
msgstr ""
"Un crustacé ayant l'air d'un homard miniature, et très bon cuit dans une "
"marmite avec des épices."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "crustacean larva"
msgid_plural "crustacean larvae"
msgstr[0] "larve de crustacé"
msgstr[1] "larves de crustacé"
msgstr[2] "larves de crustacé"

#. ~ Description of monster "crustacean larva"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A minuscule half-translucent crustacean larva.  Impossible to identify which"
" species it belongs to."
msgstr ""
"Une larve de crustacé presque translucide, il est complètement impossible "
"d'identifier précisement à quelle espèce elle appartient."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "American eel"
msgid_plural "American eels"
msgstr[0] "anguille américaine"
msgstr[1] "anguilles américaines"
msgstr[2] "anguilles américaines"

#. ~ Description of monster "American eel"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"An American eel.  They used to be quite common in these parts until the dams"
" were built.  They'll get a second chance now that those aren't running."
msgstr ""
"Une anguille américaine, commune dans les environs avant la construction de "
"masse de barrages, mais sa population va peut être rebondir maintenant que "
"ceux-ci ne fonctionnent plus."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "oversized crayfish"
msgid_plural "oversized crayfish"
msgstr[0] "écrevisse géante"
msgstr[1] "écrevisses géantes"
msgstr[2] "écrevisses géantes"

#. ~ Description of monster "oversized crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A mutant crayfish the size of a dog, with a brown carapace, claws, and long "
"antennae."
msgstr ""
"Une écrevisse mutante de la taille d'un chien possédant une carapace brune, "
"des pinces menaçantes et de longues antennes."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/fish.json
msgid "giant crayfish"
msgid_plural "giant crayfish"
msgstr[0] "écrevisse gigantesque"
msgstr[1] "écrevisses gigantesques"
msgstr[2] "écrevisses gigantesques"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A mutant, terrestrial variety of crayfish, this massive crustacean resembles"
" a humongous lobster."
msgstr ""
"Une écrevisse terrestre gigantesque ressemblant à un homard de taille "
"mythique."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/fish.json
msgid "colossal crayfish"
msgid_plural "colossal crayfish"
msgstr[0] "écrevisse colossale"
msgstr[1] "écrevisses colossales"
msgstr[2] "écrevisses colossales"

#. ~ Description of monster "colossal crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "An enormous mutated gray crayfish with pincer claws and long antennae."
msgstr ""
"Une écrevisse mutante énorme munie de pinces redoutables et de longues "
"antennes."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/fish.json
msgid "giant crayfish larva"
msgid_plural "giant crayfish larvae"
msgstr[0] "larve d'écrevisse géante"
msgstr[1] "larves d'écrevisse géantes"
msgstr[2] "larves d'écrevisse géantes"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant crayfish larva"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A large crayfish larva already larger than non-mutated adults of its kind."
msgstr ""
"Une larve d'écrevisse mutante gigantesque déjà plus large que les adultes "
"non-mutants de son espèce."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "razorclaw"
msgid_plural "razorclaws"
msgstr[0] "pince-rasoir"
msgstr[1] "pince-rasoirs"
msgstr[2] "pince-rasoirs"

#. ~ Description of monster "razorclaw"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A man-sized crustacean clad in iron-like chitin, capable of emitting "
"horrible shrieking noises.  Often spotted near shipwrecks or other dark, "
"damp places, which it uses as nesting grounds."
msgstr ""
"Un crustacé mutant de la taille d'un homme adulte possédant une carapace en "
"chitine épaisse et très résistante, capable d'émettre des crissements "
"horribles avec ses mandibules. Cet monstruosité préfère fréquenter les "
"épaves ou autres endroits similairement humides et sombres pouvant être "
"utilisés comme sites de ponte."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "giant carp"
msgid_plural "giant carps"
msgstr[0] "carpe gigantesque"
msgstr[1] "carpes gigantesques"
msgstr[2] "carpes gigantesques"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant carp"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"This thing looks like a carp, but huge and very, very angry.  Death is the "
"gift of the carp god."
msgstr ""
"Cette chose à l'apparence d'une carpe, mais absolument gigantesque et "
"vraiment, vraiment très susceptible, votre mort sera une bonne offrande pour"
" le dieu des carpes."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "giant salmon"
msgid_plural "giant salmons"
msgstr[0] "saumon gigantesque"
msgstr[1] "saumons gigantesques"
msgstr[2] "saumons gigantesques"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant salmon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A mutated salmon, the size of a large dog and quite dangerous to the "
"inexperienced angler."
msgstr ""
"Un saumon mutant de la taille d'un gros chien et très dangereux pour le "
"pêcheur du dimanche."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "seweranha"
msgid_plural "seweranhas"
msgstr[0] "piranha d'égout"
msgstr[1] "piranhas d'égout"
msgstr[2] "piranhas d'égout"

#. ~ Description of monster "seweranha"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A large, mutant variety of carp.  It has shimmering green scales and a mouth"
" lined with three jagged rows of razor-sharp teeth."
msgstr ""
"Un carpe mutante doté d'écailles vert luisant et d'une gueule bordée de "
"trois rangées de dents aiguisées comme des rasoirs."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "fungal blossom"
msgid_plural "fungal blossoms"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal blossom"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"A broad fungus, looking much like a glowing blue sunflower.  It appears to "
"emit finer spores than the typical fungal emission."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "fungal hedgerow"
msgid_plural "fungal hedgerows"
msgstr[0] "haie mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "haies mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "haies mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal hedgerow"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"Looking at first glance like a dull gray privet, this \"hedge\" is really a "
"mass of barbed fungal tendrils, defending the fungal tower."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Death message of monster "fungal hedgerow"
#. ~ Death message of monster "fungal wall"
#. ~ Death message of monster "spore cloud"
#. ~ Death message of monster "ancient red dragon"
#. ~ Death message of monster "vengeance spirit"
#. ~ Death message of monster "will-o-wisp"
#. ~ Death message of monster "flying shark"
#. ~ Death message of monster "endless snake"
#. ~ Death message of monster "swarm of teeth"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json data/json/monsters/misc.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/nightmares_and_chimeras.json
#, c-format
msgid "The %s disintegrates!"
msgstr "Le %s se désintègre!"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "fungal tendril"
msgid_plural "fungal tendrils"
msgstr[0] "vrille mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "vrilles mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "vrilles mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal tendril"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "A long and delicate-looking tendril with a sharp tip."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal wall"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"A veritable wall of fungus, grown as a natural defense by the fungal spire."
"  New spores erupt from the surface every few seconds, and tendrils "
"constrict around it, pulling new mass into its shape.  They move with an "
"inexorable strength that could snap limbs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json data/mods/CrazyCataclysm/crazy_monsters.json
msgid "fungaloid"
msgid_plural "fungaloids"
msgstr[0] "mycelloïde"
msgstr[1] "mycelloïdes"
msgstr[2] "mycelloïdes"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungaloid"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"A pale white fungus, one meaty gray stalk supporting a bloom at the top.  "
"Spores are periodically expelled from its gills, and a few tendrils extend "
"from the base, allowing mobility and some basic means of defense."
msgstr ""
"Un fongus pâle blanc, une tige charnue grise avec une fleur en haut. Ses "
"branchies crachent des spores périodiquement, et des vrilles étendent sa "
"base, lui permettant de se mouvoir et comme moyen de défense rudimentaire."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "fungaloid shambler"
msgid_plural "fungaloid shamblers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "fungaloid shambler"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"A large white fungus, a bulging gray stalk supporting a bloom at the top.  "
"Spores float from its gills and tendrils extend from the base.  Chunks of "
"rock, metal, bone, and wood are held by tendrils as a kind of armor."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of special attack of monster "fungaloid shambler"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "The fungaloid shambler throws a rock!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "fungal spire"
msgid_plural "fungal spires"
msgstr[0] "cathédrale mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "cathédrales mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "cathédrales mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal spire"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"An enormous fungal spire, towering over the ground.  It pulsates slowly, "
"continuously growing new defenses."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "giant fungal blossom"
msgid_plural "giant fungal blossoms"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "giant fungal blossom"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"An immense fungal blossom, towering over its surroundings.  It pulses with a"
" soft blue glow, continuously pumping its spores into the air."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_fungal.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/mods/alt_map_key/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "fungal tower"
msgid_plural "fungal towers"
msgstr[0] "tour mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "tours mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "tours mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal tower"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"An enormous fungal tower.  On closer inspection, its cap is supported by "
"LOTS of fungal tendrils of various thicknesses, emerging from yet more "
"bristling tendrils at ground level.  Between this redundancy and their "
"noticeable movement creating frequent gaps, it's tough to get a solid shot "
"on the thing."
msgstr ""
"Une énorme tour fongique. Son chapeau est maintenu par de nombreuses vrilles"
" de tailles diverses et des racines hérissés. Ses mouvement saccadés le "
"rendent difficile à toucher."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "fungal sporeling"
msgid_plural "fungal sporelings"
msgstr[0] "sporeling mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "sporelings mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "sporelings mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal sporeling"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"A fungal stalk several feet in height.  Two vicious-looking tendrils extend "
"from its thorned and leathery exterior, and it moves about faster than the "
"larger fungaloids."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json data/mods/no_fungal_growth/modinfo.json
msgid "spore cloud"
msgid_plural "spore clouds"
msgstr[0] "nuage de spores"
msgstr[1] "nuages de spores"
msgstr[2] "nuages de spores"

#. ~ Description of monster "spore cloud"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "A mass of spores the size of a balled fist, wafting around in the air."
msgstr "Un amas de spores de la taille d'un poing, se baladant dans l'air."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "fungal ant"
msgid_plural "fungal ants"
msgstr[0] "fourmi mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "fourmis mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "fourmis mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal ant"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"Pale, sickly gray in color, this giant ant's cracked exoskeleton is barely "
"held together by coils of fungus erupting from every joint in its body."
msgstr ""
"L'exosquelette d'une pâleur grise maladive et fendu de cette fourmi géante "
"est à peine maintenu en un morceau par des fonges qui jaillissent des "
"articulations de l'animal."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "fungal spider"
msgid_plural "fungal spiders"
msgstr[0] "araignée mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "araignées mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "araignées mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal spider"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"The abdomen of this sickly-looking giant spider is now home to many lumps of"
" blooming fungi.  It leaves behind a trail of tainted secretions as it "
"struggles to drag itself along the ground."
msgstr ""
"L'abdomen de cette araignée géante à l'apparence pitoyable est maintenant "
"l'hôte de nombreuses taches de champignons proliférants et sa marche "
"laborieuse laisse derrière elle une trainée de soie moisie lorsque ces "
"filières heurtent le sol."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid "fungal zombie"
msgid_plural "fungal zombies"
msgstr[0] "zombie mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "zombies mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "zombies mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal zombie"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid ""
"Once alive, then undead, now something else entirely.  Fungal tendrils "
"sprout from its mouth, eyes, and other orifices, holding together a "
"shambling mass of mold-covered flesh."
msgstr ""
"D'abord vivant, puis mort-vivant et maintenant quelque chose d'autre. Vous "
"observez des croissances fongiques poussant de sa bouche, de ses yeux et "
"d'autres orifices naturels ou non, peinant à garder entière une masse "
"trébuchante de chair moisie repoussante."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid "bloated fungal zombie"
msgid_plural "bloated fungal zombies"
msgstr[0] "zombie ballonné mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "zombies ballonnés mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "zombies ballonnés mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "bloated fungal zombie"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid ""
"With its swollen gray skin overgrown by thick layer of mold, this balloon-"
"like fungal zombie looks like it could violently burst into a cloud of "
"noxious spores at any moment."
msgstr ""
"La chair gonflée et grisâtre de ce zombie couvert d'une épaisse couche de "
"moisissure à l'air d'être capable d'exploser à tout moment en un vaste nuage"
" de spores nocives."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid "pollinator zombie"
msgid_plural "pollinator zombies"
msgstr[0] "zombie pollinisateur"
msgstr[1] "zombies pollinisateurs"
msgstr[2] "zombies pollinisateurs"

#. ~ Description of monster "pollinator zombie"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid ""
"Every breath of this crooked, fungus-ridden zombie emits a fine dust of "
"spores, and it constantly looks like it's emerging from a cloud of mist."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid "fungal skeletal zombie"
msgid_plural "fungal skeletal zombies"
msgstr[0] "zombie ossifié mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "zombies ossifiés mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "zombies ossifiés mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal skeletal zombie"
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal skeletal brute"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid ""
"Fungi bloom from the crevices in the twisted bone growths that cover this "
"creature.  Spores linger in the air around it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid "fungal skeletal brute"
msgid_plural "fungal skeletal brutes"
msgstr[0] "brute ossifiée mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "brutes ossifiées mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "brutes ossifiées mycellaires"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid "fungal juggernaut"
msgid_plural "fungal juggernauts"
msgstr[0] "mastodonte ossifié mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "mastodontes ossifiés mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "mastodontes ossifiés mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal juggernaut"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid ""
"Fungi bloom from the crevices in the ossified plates of this ponderous bone "
"titan, and it seems even its eyes are lost to it.  A dust of spores lands on"
" the ground with every sluggish stomp of its heavy legs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid "fungal child"
msgid_plural "fungal children"
msgstr[0] "enfant mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "enfants mycellaire"
msgstr[2] "enfants mycellaire"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal child"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid ""
"It is hard to recognize a human child in this creature.  Disgusting-looking "
"mold covers most of its skin.  Many cracks perforate its body, with small "
"fungal stalks poking through."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid "fungal boomer"
msgid_plural "fungal boomers"
msgstr[0] "boomer mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "boomers mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "boomers mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal boomer"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid ""
"A rotund and bloated human body with pasty, fungus-ridden flesh.  Its mouth "
"drips with a frothing gray sludge."
msgstr ""
"Un humain rond et gras en décomposition, avec la chair infestée par les "
"spores. Un liquide grisâtre et mousseux s'écoule de sa bouche."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid "fungal wretch"
msgid_plural "fungal wretches"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal wretch"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid ""
"This severely deformed child lies on its back, its ribs exposed to the sky."
"  With its limbs contorted in ways only possible through a lack of bones, "
"the child’s ribcage stretches far beyond the boundaries of human biology, "
"appearing akin to a bony hive coated in quivering fungal matter.  Spores "
"occasionally waft from its hollowed interior, and, periodically, you can "
"catch sight of weak movement within the abomination’s guts."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "fungal wretch"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid ""
"Through a plume of fungal spores, a small beast struggles to take flight "
"from the wretch’s abdomen!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid "fungal raptor"
msgid_plural "fungal raptors"
msgstr[0] "raptor mycellaire"
msgstr[1] "raptors mycellaires"
msgstr[2] "raptors mycellaires"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal raptor"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus_zombie.json
msgid ""
"Infested by a thick crust of fungal growth, this small, winged predator "
"darts through the air on three spongy wings that look like stretched human "
"hands.  A sheer, jagged spike juts out from the point where the wings meet."
"  It looks like nothing you've seen on Earth, and yet strangely like it is "
"made of human parts."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "larva"
msgid_plural "larvae"
msgstr[0] "larve"
msgstr[1] "larves"
msgstr[2] "larves"

#. ~ Description of monster "larva"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "A fake monster.  If you're seeing this something went wrong."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "dark wyrm"
msgid_plural "dark wyrms"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "dark wyrm"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A huge mutated worm living deep underground.  It has a round, gaping mouth "
"lined with dagger-like teeth, and its flesh is slick with bubbling blue "
"slime."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "graboid"
msgid_plural "graboids"
msgstr[0] "graboid"
msgstr[1] "graboids"
msgstr[2] "graboids"

#. ~ Description of monster "graboid"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A monstrous beast the size of a semi truck with a tripartite mouth that "
"opens to reveal hundreds of writhing tongues with razor sharp edges.  It "
"keeps most of its enormous body hidden underground."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Death message of monster "graboid"
#. ~ Death message of monster "giant worm"
#. ~ Death message of monster "slime"
#. ~ Death message of monster "brain slime"
#. ~ Death message of monster "big slime"
#. ~ Death message of monster "zombie hollow"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json data/json/monsters/slimes.json
#: data/json/monsters/zed_misc.json
#, c-format
msgid "The %s splits in two!"
msgstr "Le %s se sépare en deux!"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "half worm"
msgid_plural "half worms"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "half worm"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "A squiggling severed portion of a wounded giant worm."
msgstr "Un morceau ondulant coupé d'un ver géant blessé."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "giant worm"
msgid_plural "giant worms"
msgstr[0] "ver géant"
msgstr[1] "vers géants"
msgstr[2] "vers géants"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant worm"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A huge, mutated creature that might once have been a nightcrawler.  It "
"possesses a large fanged mouth and a long slender body that comes up to your"
" shoulder, with even more surely hiding underground."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "large worm"
msgid_plural "large worms"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "large worm"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A disturbingly large mutated subterranean creature similar to a "
"nightcrawler.  It possesses a fanged mouth and a long slender body that "
"comes up to your knees, with even more surely hiding underground."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "earthworm larva"
msgid_plural "earthworm larvae"
msgstr[0] "larve de ver de terre"
msgstr[1] "larves de ver de terre"
msgstr[2] "larves de ver de terre"

#. ~ Description of monster "earthworm larva"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "A white wriggling worm."
msgstr ""
"Un ver de terre juvénile à la couleur laiteuse de taille impressionnante."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "cockroach"
msgid_plural "cockroaches"
msgstr[0] "cafard géant"
msgstr[1] "cafards géants"
msgstr[2] "cafards géants"

#. ~ Description of monster "cockroach"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "An aggressive mutant cockroach the size of a small dog."
msgstr "Un cafard mutant agressif de la taille d'un petit chien."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "skittering plague"
msgid_plural "skittering plagues"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "skittering plague"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A giant, sickly-looking cockroach that appears to be using the undead as its"
" primary food source.  The diet of infected flesh doesn't seem to harm it, "
"but something about the roach's biology is clearly changing.  It doesn't "
"seem interested in you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "plague nymph"
msgid_plural "plague nymphs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "plague nymph"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A sickly-looking mutant cockroach about the size of a rat, raised from birth"
" on a healthy diet of zombie flesh.  It still has enough natural instinct "
"left to avoid approaching you."
msgstr ""
"Un cafard mutant de la taille d'un rat ayant l'air cadavérique du à son "
"alimentation depuis la naissance consistant uniquement de viande de zombie, "
"malgré cela, cette monstruosité a toujours assez d'instinct de conservation "
"pour ne pas s'approcher de vous."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "plague vector"
msgid_plural "plague vectors"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "plague vector"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"This giant cockroach has been feeding on the undead for some time and "
"started to mutate chaotically.  Extra limbs and growths sprout from its "
"thorax, and it is notably aggressive even to creatures much larger than "
"itself."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "giant cockroach"
msgid_plural "giant cockroaches"
msgstr[0] "cafard gigantesque"
msgstr[1] "cafards gigantesques"
msgstr[2] "cafards gigantesques"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant cockroach"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A mutant cockroach the size of a dog.  This size advantage is apparently all"
" it needs to start regarding humans as food!"
msgstr ""
"Un cafard mutant de la taille d'un chien, à cette taille, cette abomination "
"a apparemment décider d'ajouter l'homme à son menu!"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "giant cockroach nymph"
msgid_plural "giant cockroach nymphs"
msgstr[0] "nymphe de cafard gigantesque"
msgstr[1] "nymphes de cafard gigantesque"
msgstr[2] "nymphes de cafard gigantesque"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant cockroach nymph"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "A baby mutant cockroach about the size of a rat."
msgstr "Un cafard nouveau-né de la taille d'un rat."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "pregnant giant cockroach"
msgid_plural "pregnant giant cockroaches"
msgstr[0] "cafard gigantesque enceinte"
msgstr[1] "cafards gigantesques enceintes"
msgstr[2] "cafards gigantesques enceintes"

#. ~ Description of monster "pregnant giant cockroach"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A mutant cockroach the size of a small dog.  Its abdomen is heavily swollen "
"with eggs."
msgstr ""
"Un cafard mutant de la taille d'un petit chien, son abdomen plein à craquer "
"d'œufs."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "bee"
msgid_plural "bees"
msgstr[0] "abeille géante"
msgstr[1] "abeilles géantes"
msgstr[2] "abeilles géantes"

#. ~ Description of monster "bee"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "A mutant bee the size of a small dog."
msgstr "Une abeille mutante de la taille d'un chien."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "giant bee"
msgid_plural "giant bees"
msgstr[0] "abeille gigantesque"
msgstr[1] "abeilles gigantesques"
msgstr[2] "abeilles gigantesques"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant bee"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"With a stinger the size of a kitchen knife, this dog-sized insect's black "
"and yellow markings warn you to leave it undisturbed."
msgstr ""
"Avec un dard de la taille d'un couteau de cuisine, cet insecte grand comme "
"un chien, présente des marques jaunes vous prévenant de le laisser "
"tranquille."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "alpha bee"
msgid_plural "alpha bees"
msgstr[0] "abeille alpha"
msgstr[1] "abeilles alpha"
msgstr[2] "abeilles alpha"

#. ~ Description of monster "alpha bee"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"An enormous mutant bee with black and white markings and a long stinger "
"spelling doom."
msgstr ""
"Une abeille mutante énorme recouverte de marques noires et blanches doté "
"d'un dard tellement long et effilé qu'il pourrait être appelé une épée."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "centipede"
msgid_plural "centipedes"
msgstr[0] "centipède"
msgstr[1] "centipèdes"
msgstr[2] "centipèdes"

#. ~ Description of monster "centipede"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A brightly-colored mutant centipede the size of a small dog, skittering "
"quickly in the underbrush.  Probably won't think you're suitable prey, but "
"beware its venom."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "giant centipede"
msgid_plural "giant centipedes"
msgstr[0] "centipède gigantesque"
msgstr[1] "centipèdes gigantesques"
msgstr[2] "centipèdes gigantesques"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant centipede"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A two-meter-long centipede with a menacing set of venom-dripping mandibles "
"and a worrying number of grabbing appendages, moving swiftly on dozens of "
"spindly legs.  It has a pair of small compound eyes, but seems to mostly "
"orient itself with its antennae."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "centipede larva"
msgid_plural "centipede larvae"
msgstr[0] "larve de centipède"
msgstr[1] "larves de centipède"
msgstr[2] "larves de centipède"

#. ~ Description of monster "centipede larva"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A juvenile centipede.  Despite its young age it is still quite large and you"
" reckon these mandibles could pack quite a bite."
msgstr ""
"Un centipède juvénile. Malgré son jeune age il reste assez gros et vous "
"devriez probablement faire attention à ses mandibules."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "centipede matriarch"
msgid_plural "centipede matriarchs"
msgstr[0] "matriarche centipède"
msgstr[1] "matriarches centipèdes"
msgstr[2] "matriarches centipèdes"

#. ~ Description of monster "centipede matriarch"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A giant centipede grown even larger, hind segments curled up to protect a "
"huge clump of eggs and its children of different ages.  Sometimes one of its"
" young gets shaken off by its clutchmates and disappears into the "
"underbrush."
msgstr ""
"Un centipède géant devenu encore plus large, ses segments antérieurs "
"enroulés pour protéger un amas d'œufs énorme couvert de sa progéniture à "
"différents stades de développement. Parfois l'un de ceux-ci se fait expulsé "
"par sa fratrie et s'enfuit hors de vue."

#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "centipede matriarch"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "A small centipede is shaken off in the struggle!"
msgstr "Un petit centipède est expulsé durant la lutte!"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "armored centipede"
msgid_plural "armored centipedes"
msgstr[0] "centipède géant blindé"
msgstr[1] "centipèdes géants blindés"
msgstr[2] "centipèdes géants blindés"

#. ~ Description of monster "armored centipede"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A huge mutated centipede covered in interlocking chitinous plates of "
"metallic gray, reminding you more of a runaway train car than any living "
"animal.  Its mandibles end in jagged points, seemingly specialised to hunt "
"prey at least as well-armored as itself.  You really don't want to try if "
"you'd fare better."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "giant dragonfly naiad"
msgid_plural "giant dragonfly naiads"
msgstr[0] "naïade de libellule géante"
msgstr[1] "naïades de libellule géantes"
msgstr[2] "naïades de libellule géantes"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant dragonfly naiad"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A predatory, aquatic dragonfly larva, normally barely a centimeter long and "
"feeding on small fishes, grown to the size of a catfish.  Underneath its "
"sharp mandibles you can see that its folded lower jaw has changed into "
"something resembling a barbed spear."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "giant dragonfly"
msgid_plural "giant dragonflies"
msgstr[0] "libellule géante"
msgstr[1] "libellules géantes"
msgstr[2] "libellules géantes"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant dragonfly"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A ferocious, bright green dragonfly, still lightning-fast despite growing to"
" the size of a schoolchild.  Its head is little more than a basketball-sized"
" pair of rainbow compound eyes, and its legs - already specialized for "
"grasping prey - end in curved talons."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "fused dragonflies"
msgid_plural "fused dragonflies"
msgstr[0] "libellules géantes accouplées"
msgstr[1] "libellules géantes accouplées"
msgstr[2] "libellules géantes accouplées"

#. ~ Description of monster "fused dragonflies"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"What appears to be a single, enormous insect with a swollen abdomen is "
"actually the unholy union of two dragonflies in the act of mating, bodies "
"still locked into the telltale heart shape.  The remains of their wings and "
"abdomens form an egg sac they sluggishly pull between them, periodically "
"dropping a handful of glistening eggs."
msgstr ""
"Bien que cette abomination de loin à l'air d'être un seul énorme insecte "
"doté d'un abdomen ballonné, un second coup d'œil révèle que ceci est un "
"couple de libellules mutantes coincées dans leur position de reproduction en"
" forme de cœur, ce qui reste de leurs ailes et de leurs abdomens ayant formé"
" un sac d'œufs qu'elles peinent à trainer derrière elles, duquel s'échappe "
"périodiquement une poignée d'œufs luisants."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "firefly"
msgid_plural "fireflies"
msgstr[0] "luciole géante"
msgstr[1] "lucioles géantes"
msgstr[2] "lucioles géantes"

#. ~ Description of monster "firefly"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A mutated firefly grown to the size of a large housecat, brightly glowing "
"abdomen bobbing up and down as it tries to impress its unseen mate.  It "
"looks strangely uninterested in you and everything else."
msgstr ""
"Une luciole mutante de la taille d'un gros chat, son abdomen luisant ce "
"trémoussant pour essayer d'attirer un partenaire en ignorant le monde autour"
" d'elle."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "firefly larva"
msgid_plural "firefly larvae"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "firefly larva"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"An oversized larva of a firefly.  Shockingly large when compared to the "
"adults of its kind."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "fly"
msgid_plural "flies"
msgstr[0] "mouche géante"
msgstr[1] "mouches géantes"
msgstr[2] "mouches géantes"

#. ~ Description of monster "fly"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A mutant housefly the size of a small dog.  Its buzzing is high-pitched and "
"somehow sad."
msgstr ""
"Une mouche domestique mutante de la taille d'un petit chien. Son "
"bourdonnement aigu sonne… triste?"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "giant fly"
msgid_plural "giant flies"
msgstr[0] "mouche géante"
msgstr[1] "mouches géantes"
msgstr[2] "mouches géantes"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant fly"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A tremendous housefly the size of a dog, predictably accompanied by a loud, "
"incessant buzzing sound."
msgstr ""
"Une mouche gigantesque de la taille d'un chien émettant un bourdonnement "
"incessant."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "giant grub"
msgid_plural "giant grubs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "giant grub"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "A grub the size of a small dog."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "frigate fly"
msgid_plural "frigate flies"
msgstr[0] "mouche gargantuesque"
msgstr[1] "mouches gargantuesques"
msgstr[2] "mouches gargantuesques"

#. ~ Description of monster "frigate fly"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A mutant housefly the size of a cow, creating a loud buzzing sound as it "
"inexplicably stays airborne."
msgstr ""
"Une mouche domestique mutante de la taille d'une vache, beaucoup trop grosse"
" pour voler et néanmoins émettant un bourdonnement incessant en faisant "
"exactement ce qui devrait lui être impossible."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "mosquito"
msgid_plural "mosquitos"
msgstr[0] "moustique géant"
msgstr[1] "moustiques géants"
msgstr[2] "moustiques géants"

#. ~ Description of monster "mosquito"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A mutant mosquito the size of a small dog, buzzing and fluttering "
"erratically."
msgstr ""
"Un moustique mutant de la taille d'un petit chien, volant de façon erratique"
" en bourdonnant."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "giant mosquito"
msgid_plural "giant mosquitos"
msgstr[0] "moustique gigantesque"
msgstr[1] "moustiques gigantesques"
msgstr[2] "moustiques gigantesques"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant mosquito"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A giant mutant mosquito the size of a dog, fluttering erratically.  Its face"
" is dominated by a long, spear-tipped proboscis."
msgstr ""
"Un moustique mutant gigantesque de la taille d'un chien, doté d'une longue "
"trompe se terminant par une pointe de lance vicieuse, volant de façon "
"erratique."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "giant mosquito larva"
msgid_plural "giant mosquito larvae"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "giant mosquito larva"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A large mosquito larva.  A bit more unsettling now that it isn't "
"microscopic."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "bloodbank mosquito"
msgid_plural "bloodbank mosquitos"
msgstr[0] "moustique gargantuesque"
msgstr[1] "moustiques gargantuesques"
msgstr[2] "moustiques gargantuesques"

#. ~ Description of monster "bloodbank mosquito"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A mutant mosquito the size of a cow, with huge, thin wings and legs.  Its "
"face is dominated by a long, spear-tipped proboscis."
msgstr ""
"Un moustique mutant de la taille d'une vache, doté d'une longue trompe se "
"terminant par une pointe de lance vicieuse, ainsi que des pattes et des "
"ailes fines gigantesques."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "cellar spider"
msgid_plural "cellar spiders"
msgstr[0] "araignée de cave géante"
msgstr[1] "araignées de cave géantes"
msgstr[2] "araignées de cave géantes"

#. ~ Description of monster "cellar spider"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A cellar spider - also known as \"daddy long-legs\" - grown to distressing "
"size.  Its body is about the size of your head, with the long, spindly legs "
"raising it up to your knee.  It tries getting away from you with an "
"unnervingly fluid run."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json data/mods/Defense_Mode/monsters.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "giant cellar spider"
msgid_plural "giant cellar spiders"
msgstr[0] "araignée de cave gigantesque"
msgstr[1] "araignées de cave gigantesques"
msgstr[2] "araignées de cave gigantesques"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant cellar spider"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json data/mods/Defense_Mode/monsters.json
msgid ""
"A huge brown spider in constant movement, with a small body the size of a "
"child held up at chest level by a set of spindly legs that branch into "
"three-pronged graspers at the end.  Unlike the smaller variant it obviously "
"decided hunting you is worth a try, and follows you with mandibles "
"chittering in anticipation."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "cellar spiderling"
msgid_plural "cellar spiderlings"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "cellar spiderling"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid "A juvenile cellar spider, about the size of a beer bottle."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/insect_spider.json
msgid "mommy long-legs"
msgid_plural "mommy long legs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "mommy long-legs"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"This surprisingly shy giant cellar spider holds a head-sized ball of "
"crawling spiderlings of different ages in its mandibles, carefully balancing"
" on her long legs not to drop the precious cargo.  She seems uninterested in"
" you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Death message of monster "mommy long-legs"
#: data/json/monsters/insect_spider.json
