"dog."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "fox"
msgid_plural "foxes"
msgstr[0] "renard"
msgstr[1] "renards"
msgstr[2] "renards"

#. ~ Description of monster "fox"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A small, omnivorous canine with almost cat-like mannerisms.  It is a "
"solitary hunter, and one of the only canids able to climb trees."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "fox"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The red fox, an omnivorous canine and largest of the true foxes, it is a "
"wily hunter with a combative, suspicious temperament."
msgstr ""
"Le renard roux, un canidé omnivore et le plus gros du genre Vulpes. C'est un"
" chasseur rusé doté d'un tempérament combatif et suspicieux."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "groundhog"
msgid_plural "groundhogs"
msgstr[0] "marmotte"
msgstr[1] "marmottes"
msgstr[2] "marmottes"

#. ~ Description of monster "groundhog"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"Also known as the woodchuck, this ground squirrel has no actual talent for "
"chucking wood."
msgstr ""
"Également appelé siffleux, cet écureuil vit sur la terre ferme et siffle "
"pour prévenir ses congénères d'un danger."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "jackrabbit"
msgid_plural "jackrabbits"
msgstr[0] "lièvre"
msgstr[1] "lièvres"
msgstr[2] "lièvres"

#. ~ Description of monster "jackrabbit"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The snowshoe hare, a small grass-eater with a brown fur coat that changes to"
" white in the wintertime."
msgstr ""
"Le lièvre d'Amérique, ou lièvre à raquettes, se nourrit de plantes herbacées"
" et sa fourrure brune devient blanche en hiver."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "foal"
msgid_plural "foals"
msgstr[0] "poulain"
msgstr[1] "poulains"
msgstr[2] "poulains"

#. ~ Description of monster "foal"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A hooved grazing mammal with a mane of hair, a sweeping tail, and powerful-"
"looking muscles.  This one is still a juvenile; it'll take a while before it"
" can be ridden."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "horse"
msgid_plural "horses"
msgstr[0] "cheval"
msgstr[1] "chevaux"
msgstr[2] "chevaux"

#. ~ Description of monster "horse"
#. ~ Description of monster "Scott's horse"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#: data/mods/Megafauna/monsters/mf_domestic.json
msgid ""
"A hooved grazing mammal with a mane of hair, a sweeping tail, and powerful-"
"looking muscles.  A stalwart companion to humans for longer than recorded "
"history, with some effort you should be able to get this one to trust you "
"enough to ride it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "mon_horse_police"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A hooved grazing mammal with a mane of hair, a sweeping tail, and powerful-"
"looking muscles.  This one has been trained to have less of a fear reaction "
"in order to assist with riot control and standard police work.  With some "
"effort, you should be able to get this one to trust you enough to ride it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "lemming"
msgid_plural "lemmings"
msgstr[0] "lemming"
msgstr[1] "lemmings"
msgstr[2] "lemmings"

#. ~ Description of monster "lemming"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The Northern bog lemming, a small, predominantly vegetarian rodent that "
"spends its life in the murk of swamps and other wetlands.  Contrary to "
"popular belief, these creatures are not particularly hapless or suicidal, "
"but they can eat themselves into scarcity within a few generations."
msgstr ""
"Un petit rongeur végétarien qui passe sa vie dans les marais et la toundra. "
"Contrairement aux légendes urbaines, ils ne sont pas suicidaires, mais "
"peuvent se manger entre eux dans les grandes périodes de sécheresse."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "mink"
msgid_plural "minks"
msgstr[0] "vison"
msgstr[1] "visons"
msgstr[2] "visons"

#. ~ Description of monster "mink"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The American mink, a partially aquatic weasel, once factory-farmed for its "
"fur.  It is a capable fisher, but the presence of otters in these parts "
"makes it rely more on food from the land."
msgstr ""
"Le vison américain, une belette partiellement aquatique ayant autrefois été "
"élevée intensément pour sa fourrure. C'est un pêcheur compétent mais la "
"présence de loutre sur son territoire en Nouvelle Angleterre le rends plus "
"terrestre."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "moose"
msgid_plural "moose"
msgstr[0] "élan"
msgstr[1] "élans"
msgstr[2] "élans"

#. ~ Description of monster "moose"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The Eastern moose, the largest living species of deer.  While they aren't "
"typically aggressive unless provoked, the autumn mating season can make the "
"bulls quite ill-tempered."
msgstr ""
"L'élan de l'est, la plus grande espèce vivante de cerf. Bien que cet animal "
"ne soit pas typiquement agressif à moins d'être provoqué, leur saison de "
"reproduction en automne rends les mâles assez hargneux."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "moose calf"
msgid_plural "moose calves"
msgstr[0] "élan juvénile"
msgstr[1] "élans juvéniles"
msgstr[2] "élans juvéniles"

#. ~ Description of monster "moose calf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The baby moose is called a calf.  Calves can outrun a human within days of "
"birth and gain weight at an incredible pace."
msgstr ""
"Une jeune élan capable de courir plus vite qu'un humain quelques jours après"
" être né et de grandir à un rythme effréné."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "great tusked moose"
msgid_plural "great tusked moose"
msgstr[0] "élan à défenses"
msgstr[1] "élans à défenses"
msgstr[2] "élans à défenses"

#. ~ Description of monster "great tusked moose"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The great tusked moose is a mutant variety of megafauna that evolved after "
"the Cataclysm.  Easily recognized by the underslung tusks off the side of "
"each mouth, in addition to an impressive rack of horns.  These moose are "
"more aggressive than their predecessors."
msgstr ""
"Une espèce mutante d'élan causée par le cataclysme et aisément distinguable "
"de ses cousins normaux par la présence des défenses présentes sur les deux "
"côtés de sa bouche, leur bois massifs et acérés ainsi que leur attitude "
"beaucoup plus aggressive. "

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "tusked moose calf"
msgid_plural "tusked moose calves"
msgstr[0] "élan à défenses juvénile"
msgstr[1] "élans à défenses juvéniles"
msgstr[2] "élans à défenses juvéniles"

#. ~ Description of monster "tusked moose calf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The baby moose is called a calf so are it's tusked mutant descendants.  "
"Calves can outrun a human within days of birth and gain weight at an "
"incredible pace."
msgstr ""
"Une jeune élan capable de courir plus vite qu'un humain quelques jours après"
" être né et de grandir à un rythme effréné. Celui-ci est équipé de défenses "
"émergeant à peine de sa bouche et ayant déjà l'air vicieuses."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "muskrat"
msgid_plural "muskrats"
msgstr[0] "rat musqué"
msgstr[1] "rats musqués"
msgstr[2] "rats musqués"

#. ~ Description of monster "muskrat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A large omnivorous rodent with a thick furry pelt, found in wetlands across "
"the Northern Hemisphere.  It marks its territory with a musky odor for which"
" it is named."
msgstr ""
"Un gros rongeur omnivore équipé d'une épaisse fourrure habitant les zones "
"humides de l'hémisphère nord et marque son territoire avec son odeur "
"musquée, qui lui a donné son nom."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "opossum"
msgid_plural "opossums"
msgstr[0] "opossum"
msgstr[1] "opossums"
msgstr[2] "opossums"

#. ~ Description of monster "opossum"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The Virginia opossum, a small omnivorous marsupial native to North America."
"  About the size of a cat, it is hardy and adaptive, and a fairly common "
"sight in urban areas."
msgstr ""
"L'opossum de Virginie, un petit marsupial omnivore natif d'Amérique du nord."
" Mesurant à peu près la taille d'un chat, il est résistant et s'adapte; on "
"le croise souvent dans les zones urbaines."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "otter"
msgid_plural "otters"
msgstr[0] "loutre"
msgstr[1] "loutres"
msgstr[2] "loutres"

#. ~ Description of monster "otter"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The North American river otter, a shy water-dwelling relative of the weasel "
"that lives in large families along the banks of streams.  It is an excellent"
" fisher and a resourceful survivor, using the abandoned dens of beavers and "
"other animals to raise its own young."
msgstr ""
"Une loutre de rivière nord américaine, une cousine timide de la belette "
"vivant en larges groupes en bord de rivière. Une excellente pêcheuse mais "
"n'hésitant pas à varier son alimentation si l'opportunité se présente et "
"utilisant parfois des barrages de castor abandonnés pour abriter leurs "
"propres petits."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "piglet"
msgid_plural "piglets"
msgstr[0] "porcelet"
msgstr[1] "porcelets"
msgstr[2] "porcelets"

#. ~ Description of monster "piglet"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A domesticated omnivore descended from the wild boar, intelligent and "
"inquisitive.  Left to its own devices, it has gone feral.  Unlike the fully "
"grown version, this juvenile can be tamed."
msgstr ""
"Un omnivore domestiqué descendant des sangliers sauvage. Cet animal, curieux"
" et intelligent, est retourné à l'état sauvage en l'absence de présence "
"humaine, mais étant encore jeune, il devrait être possible pour vous de le "
"redomestiquer."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "pig"
msgid_plural "pigs"
msgstr[0] "cochon"
msgstr[1] "cochons"
msgstr[2] "cochons"

#. ~ Description of monster "pig"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A domesticated omnivore descended from the wild boar, intelligent and "
"inquisitive.  Left to its own devices, it has gone feral."
msgstr ""
"Un omnivore domestique issu des sangliers sauvages; il est curieux et "
"intelligent. Abandonné de ses maîtres, il est devenu sauvage."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "rabbit"
msgid_plural "rabbits"
msgstr[0] "lapin"
msgstr[1] "lapins"
msgstr[2] "lapins"

#. ~ Description of monster "rabbit"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A small mammal with a cute wiggling nose, a cotton ball tail, and a body "
"made of delicious flesh."
msgstr ""
"Un petit rongeur avec un mignon nez remuant, une queue ressemblant à une "
"petite boule de cotton, et une chair délicieuse."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "raccoon"
msgid_plural "raccoons"
msgstr[0] "raton laveur"
msgstr[1] "ratons laveurs"
msgstr[2] "ratons laveurs"

#. ~ Description of monster "raccoon"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A small mammal native to North America, distinctive for its dexterous paws "
"and facial markings.  It is resourceful and agile enough to open sealed "
"containers in search of food."
msgstr ""
"Un petit mammifère natif d'Amérique du Nord muni de pattes agiles et ayant "
"des marques facilement identifiables sur sa tête. Un animal très agile et "
"opportuniste ayant été capable prospérer lorsque votre civilization été "
"encore vivante et probablement toujours capable de faire de même dans ses "
"ruines."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "sewer rat"
msgid_plural "sewer rats"
msgstr[0] "rat d'égout"
msgstr[1] "rats d'égout"
msgstr[2] "rats d'égout"

#. ~ Description of monster "sewer rat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A worm-tailed rodent with long whiskers and beady eyes.  The way it squeaks "
"makes it sound… hungry."
msgstr ""
"Un rongeur ayant une queue longue et repoussante, des moustaches tordues et "
"des yeux globuleux et perçants. Les sons qu'il produit vous donne "
"l'impression que votre taille ne vous retire par de son menu."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "lamb"
msgid_plural "lambs"
msgstr[0] "agneau"
msgstr[1] "agneaux"
msgstr[2] "agneaux"

#. ~ Description of monster "lamb"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A timid, hooved grazing mammal, and one of the first animals ever "
"domesticated.  Its body is covered in a thick layer of wool."
msgstr ""
"Un mammifère à sabot timide et couvert de laine et l'un des premiers animaux"
" ayant été domestiqué par l'homme. Celui-ci est encore jeune, et ne pourra "
"probablement pas être tondu pour beaucoup de laine avant d'être adulte."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "sheep"
msgid_plural "sheep"
msgstr[0] "mouton"
msgstr[1] "moutons"
msgstr[2] "moutons"

#. ~ Description of monster "sheep"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A timid, hooved grazing mammal, and one of the first animals ever "
"domesticated.  Its body is covered in a thick layer of wool, and the males "
"have long, spiraling horns."
msgstr ""
"Un mammifère à sabot timide et couvert de laine et l'un des premiers animaux"
" ayant été domestiqué par l'homme. Les mâles sont munis de longues cornes en"
" spirale."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgctxt "goat"
msgid "kid"
msgid_plural "kids"
msgstr[0] "chevreau"
msgstr[1] "chevreaux"
msgstr[2] "chevreaux"

#. ~ Description of monster "kid"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A hooved browsing mammal known for climbing and eating just about anything."
"  The young are famously cute and cuddly."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "goat"
msgid_plural "goats"
msgstr[0] "chèvre"
msgstr[1] "chèvres"
msgstr[2] "chèvres"

#. ~ Description of monster "goat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A hooved browsing mammal known for climbing and eating just about anything."
"  Either gender can have horns."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "squirrel"
msgid_plural "squirrels"
msgstr[0] "écureuil"
msgstr[1] "écureuils"
msgstr[2] "écureuils"

#. ~ Description of monster "squirrel"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A small granivorous rodent with a long bushy tail, often seen darting amid "
"the branches of trees.  A skittish varmint with an expression of unwavering "
"austerity, it is the mortal enemy of cat and dog alike."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "squirrel"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A tiny opportunistic rodent with a long bushy tail.  The pine squirrel is "
"clever and cute, and hunted by nearly everything in the woods with a taste "
"for meat."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "weasel"
msgid_plural "weasels"
msgstr[0] "belette"
msgstr[1] "belettes"
msgstr[2] "belettes"

#. ~ Description of monster "weasel"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The long-tailed weasel, a small but ubiquitous predator whose range extends "
"across the continent.  It forms its den in small burrows, preferring to "
"occupy the nesting holes of its prey."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "wolf"
msgid_plural "wolves"
msgstr[0] "loup"
msgstr[1] "loups"
msgstr[2] "loups"

#. ~ Description of monster "wolf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A cunning pack predator, once extinct in the New England area, the wolf was "
"successfully reintroduced and their numbers reached record highs in the "
"decade before the Cataclysm.  Lucky you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "wolf puppy"
msgid_plural "wolf puppies"
msgstr[0] "louveteau"
msgstr[1] "louveteaux"
msgstr[2] "louveteaux"

#. ~ Description of monster "wolf puppy"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless wolf pup that will, in time, grow into a not-so-"
"defenseless and debatably-adorable wolf.  Be careful of its parents, who are"
" sure to be around nearby!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "reindeer"
msgid_plural "reindeer"
msgstr[0] "renne"
msgstr[1] "rennes"
msgstr[2] "rennes"

#. ~ Description of monster "reindeer"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"Also known as the caribou, this deer is native to North America and parts of"
" Eurasia.  Although usually friendly, they can be aggressive during the "
"autumn and winter mating season as well as when hungry."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "reindeer fawn"
msgid_plural "reindeer fawns"
msgstr[0] "faon de renne"
msgstr[1] "faons de renne"
msgstr[2] "faons de renne"

#. ~ Description of monster "reindeer fawn"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A juvenile caribou, it is smaller than its adult counterparts, as well as "
"having shorter antlers."
msgstr ""
"Un renne juvénile ayant une stature diminutive comparé avec ses congénères "
"adultes et équipé de bois plus petits."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "llama calf"
msgid_plural "llama calfs"
msgstr[0] "cria de lama"
msgstr[1] "crias de lama"
msgstr[2] "crias de lama"

#. ~ Description of monster "llama calf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A baby llama.  Unlike their parents, the calves tend to be more friendly in "
"demeanor."
msgstr ""
"Un bébé lama, contrairement aux adultes, celui-ci tend à être plus docile."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "llama"
msgid_plural "llama"
msgstr[0] "lama"
msgstr[1] "lamas"
msgstr[2] "lamas"

#. ~ Description of monster "llama"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A big and wooly herbivore domesticated by the Andean cultures of South "
"America.  Llamas and their kin are distant relatives to camels and are "
"adapted to mountain environments."
msgstr ""
"Un large animal laineux domestiqué par les amérindiens des Andes. Les lamas "
"et alpacas sont des cousins distant du chameaux ayant évolués pour survivre "
"dans les territoire montagneux d'Amérique du Sud."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "ferret"
msgid_plural "ferrets"
msgstr[0] "furet"
msgstr[1] "furets"
msgstr[2] "furets"

#. ~ Description of monster "ferret"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"Domesticated from the European polecat, this sleek and energetic mammal was "
"commonly kept as a pet before the Cataclysm."
msgstr ""
"Un cousin domestiqué du putois européen, ce mammifère long et énergétique "
"été un animal de compagnie populaire avant le Cataclysme."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "ferret kit"
msgid_plural "ferret kits"
msgstr[0] "fureton"
msgstr[1] "furetons"
msgstr[2] "furetons"

#. ~ Description of monster "ferret kit"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "A young domesticated ferret, known as a kit."
msgstr "Un petit furet domestiqué."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/marloss.json
msgid "Marloss zealot"
msgid_plural "Marloss zealots"
msgstr[0] "zélote du Marloss"
msgstr[1] "zélotes du Marloss"
msgstr[2] "zélotes du Marloss"

#. ~ Description of monster "Marloss zealot"
#: data/json/monsters/marloss.json
msgid ""
"Her eyes lie vacant and spittle foams in her mouth, as she recites from the "
"hymns in rapturous ecstasy."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of monster "Marloss zealot"
#: data/json/monsters/marloss.json
msgid ""
"His eyes lie vacant and spittle foams in his mouth, as he recites from the "
"hymns in rapturous ecstasy."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
msgid "X-03: 'Spectre' Recon Mech"
msgid_plural "X-03: 'Spectre' Recon Mechs"
msgstr[0] "X-03: Méca Éclaireur \"Spectre\""
msgstr[1] "X-03: Mécas Éclaireurs \"Spectre\""
msgstr[2] "X-03: Mécas Éclaireurs \"Spectre\""

#. ~ Description of monster "X-03: 'Spectre' Recon Mech"
#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
msgid ""
"The Boeing-Daewoo RMES (Recon Mechanical Exoskeleton Suit), a recent "
"acquisition by the U.S. military, it was designed to be used in a scout-"
"recon-sniper role, due to its mobility, integrated laser sniper rifle, and "
"suite of optics for target designation and battlefield awareness.  It was "
"not deployed before the Cataclysm hit, though there were a few prototypes in"
" the field.  You may be able to hack it to accept you as its pilot.  Like "
"all mech-suits, it can act as a UPS from its large battery."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
msgid "X-02: 'Grunt' Combat Mech"
msgid_plural "X-02: 'Grunt' Combat Mechs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "X-02: 'Grunt' Combat Mech"
#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
msgid ""
"The Boeing-Daewoo CMES (Combat Mechanical Exoskeleton Suit), a recent "
"acquisition by the U.S. military, it was designed to be used in a fire "
"support role, due to its fearsome integrated gatling laser.  It was not "
"deployed before the Cataclysm hit, though there were a few prototypes in the"
