msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "warped lumberjack's bag"
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid ""
"This bag shimmers before your eyes, glinting in perfectly vertical slivers "
"of purplish light.  No matter how much you pack into it, it never seems to "
"grow heavier, and its interior is a great yawning gullet of space the items "
"seem to simply disappear into.  It seems a remarkably picky eater, however, "
"and will only swallow up planks, boards, wood panels, sticks, and similar "
"wooden construction items.  It also outright refuses to be packed inside of "
"other bags."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid "warped excavator's bag"
msgid_plural "warped excavator's bags"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "warped excavator's bag"
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid ""
"This bag shimmers before your eyes, glinting in perfectly vertical slivers "
"of purplish light.  No matter how much you pack into it, it never seems to "
"grow heavier, and its interior is a great yawning gullet of space the items "
"seem to simply disappear into.  This is surely the biggest of its type.  It "
"seems a remarkably picky eater, however, and will only swallow up soil, "
"sand, gravel, clay, and most common stones.  It does seem, however, to also "
"yield to a handful of construction materials like raw limestone, cement, "
"concrete, and mortar, to name a few.  It also outright refuses to be packed "
"inside of other bags."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid "warped scrapper's bag"
msgid_plural "warped scrapper's bags"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "warped scrapper's bag"
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid ""
"This bag shimmers before your eyes, glinting in perfectly vertical slivers "
"of purplish light.  No matter how much you pack into it, it never seems to "
"grow heavier, and its interior is a great yawning gullet of space the items "
"seem to simply disappear into.  It is a remarkably picky eater, however, and"
" seems to yearn for lumps of raw metal like steel and scrap.  It does, "
"however, also yield to a few particularly dense processed forms, like pipes,"
" sheet metal, steel frames, and metal plating.  It also outright refuses to "
"be packed inside of other bags."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid "warped hauler's harness"
msgid_plural "warped hauler's harnesses"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "warped hauler's harness"
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid ""
"A looped pair of shimmering blue-black straps that can be worn over the "
"shoulders like a harness.  They make hauling effortless, and one could "
"easily cart home anything from an engine block to a bull moose with this, "
"while still keeping hands free.  The downside is that no matter how you "
"might try, they only seem to be able to support a single item.  It also "
"outright refuses to be packed inside of other bags."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid "earthbound pill"
msgid_plural "earthbound pills"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "earthbound pill"
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This pseudomagical pill extends the amount of time you can stay earthside by"
" 4 pulses, or about 50% of a normal trip.  They're precious, but should help"
" buy time for a difficult extract."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid "homeward mote"
msgid_plural "homeward motes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "homeward mote"
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid ""
"Though visibly little more than a glowing dustbunny, this strange ethereal mote of warp essence reveals, on closer inspection, something more.  A tiny, twisting, half-visible thread of shimmering bluish-purple trails away into the sky and far out of sight, unimpeded by any obstacles.\n"
"\n"
"Taking this rare and valuable artifact with you on an expedition is essentially buying life insurance.  If you die with this mote in your inventory, you will instead be restored to full health and brought home, WITH all items and equipment carried.  But this effect will only last for a single expedition.  Even if you extract safely, any and all motes carried on your person when you return home will be DESTROYED."
msgstr ""

#. ~ "description" action message of item "homeward mote"
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid "A hasty escape."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid "warped animal carrier"
msgid_plural "warped animal carriers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "warped animal carrier"
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid ""
"A hand-sized cage with a shimmering portal at its aperture.  Despite being "
"shaped more like a cat carrier, the power of warp enables it to capture "
"creatures far bigger than you.  This may be your best bet for bringing "
"animals home to your island sanctuary.  Activate to capture an adjacent "
"animal, or to release a carried animal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid "Autodoc copyplate (inert)"
msgid_plural "Autodoc copyplates (inert)"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "Autodoc copyplate (inert)"
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid ""
"This strange obsidian-colored plate is capable of mimicking the advanced "
"tech found within a modern Autodoc, and can be used to create a working copy"
" at your sanctuary.  However, it is inert in its current state and must "
"first be imprinted on a working Autodoc.  To do so, find an Autodoc during "
"an expedition and use the construction menu to imprint this plate."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid "Autodoc copyplate (activated)"
msgid_plural "Autodoc copyplates (activated)"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "Autodoc copyplate (activated)"
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid ""
"This strange obsidian-colored plate is capable of mimicking the advanced "
"tech found within a modern Autodoc, and can be used to create a working copy"
" at your sanctuary.  It has been successfully activated and can be used as "
"the catalyst to create a new Autodoc at a location of your choosing using "
"the construction menu.  Be aware this cannot be safely moved once placed, "
"and will also require you to add an adjacent couch, then convert it to an "
"Autodoc couch."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid "warped grass seeds"
msgid_plural "warped grass seeds"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "warped grass seeds"
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid ""
"While these are certainly imbued with warp, they don't seem to have any "
"supernatural powers beyond just growing quickly.  A nice option if you want "
"to re-plant grass on your island, for decoration's sake."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid "warp shards"
msgid_plural "warp shards"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of "warp shards"
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/warpitems.json
msgid ""
"A small quantity of airy-thin material that resembles flaked obsidian.  It "
"glints with a purplish shimmer that seems to stretch off the bounds of "
"itself and into the air itself.  Offered to the powers that be, one could "
"exchange it for valuable artifacts."
msgstr ""

